---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Playbooks"
  description="Step-by-step guides for opening onshore investment accounts in China as a foreigner, including what to say at the counter and what to do if you are refused."
>
  <section class="section">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="hero__eyebrow">Step by step</p>
    <h1 style="margin-top:.6rem">Playbooks</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Each playbook is written for the moment you are standing in a branch, not for the moment you
      are browsing. Materials, scripts, refusals, and how to get out again.
    </p>

    <div class="grid grid--2" style="margin-top:2rem">
      <a class="card card--link" href="/playbooks/inbound-funding">
        <span class="card__kicker">Start here</span>
        <h2 class="card__title" style="font-size:1.3rem">How money actually gets into China</h2>
        <p class="card__body">
          Current account versus capital account, what individuals can and cannot do, and the routes
          institutions use. Read this before you wire anything.
        </p>
      </a>

      <a class="card card--link" href="/playbooks/a-shares">
        <span class="card__kicker">Equities</span>
        <h2 class="card__title" style="font-size:1.3rem">Opening an A-share account</h2>
        <p class="card__body">
          Who qualifies, what to bring, the one question that saves a wasted day, and what to do when
          a branch says no.
        </p>
      </a>

      <a class="card card--link" href="/playbooks/bank-wealth">
        <span class="card__kicker">Wealth products</span>
        <h2 class="card__title" style="font-size:1.3rem">Buying bank wealth products</h2>
        <p class="card__body">
          The risk questionnaire is the real gate. How to read the prospectus, and why “expected
          return” is marketing.
        </p>
      </a>

      <a class="card card--link" href="/playbooks/funds">
        <span class="card__kicker">Funds</span>
        <h2 class="card__title" style="font-size:1.3rem">Your first fund account</h2>
        <p class="card__body">
          The widest shelf available to a foreign resident, the onboarding step that breaks, and a
          CNY 100 way to test the plumbing.
        </p>
      </a>

      <a class="card card--link" href="/playbooks/bank-account">
        <span class="card__kicker">Before all of the above</span>
        <h2 class="card__title" style="font-size:1.3rem">Opening a bank account</h2>
        <p class="card__body">
          The account every other channel settles through: which branch, what to bring, and the tax
          residency form they will put in front of you.
        </p>
      </a>

      <a class="card card--link" href="/playbooks/bonds-and-deposits">
        <span class="card__kicker">The boring middle</span>
        <h2 class="card__title" style="font-size:1.3rem">Bonds, deposits and savings bonds</h2>
        <p class="card__body">
          The channels a foreign resident can actually open and fund from RMB income — what each costs,
          and where deposit insurance stops.
        </p>
      </a>

      <a class="card card--link" href="/playbooks/etf-and-index">
        <span class="card__kicker">Cheapest equity access</span>
        <h2 class="card__title" style="font-size:1.3rem">Buying an ETF</h2>
        <p class="card__body">
          Index first, fund second, premium third. The mechanics, the costs, and the cross-border trap
          that costs people 5–10% without them noticing.
        </p>
      </a>
    </div>

    <div class="callout callout--info" style="margin-top:2rem">
      <p class="callout__title">What a playbook is not</p>
      <p class="small">
        It is not a recommendation to open any particular account or buy any particular product. It is
        a description of the process, the documents and the failure modes — so that you can decide
        with fewer surprises.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
</BaseLayout>
